## Control {{controlId}}: Manage Information System Identifiers (Assigning, Selecting, Reusing, Disabling)

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization manages information system identifiers within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Entra ID user lifecycle management, account provisioning procedures, and periodic access reviews managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if userCount}}
**Identifier Inventory:**
{{userCount}} user identifiers are managed in the tenant directory. User principal names (UPNs) serve as the unique identifier for all system access:
{{#if users}}
{{#each users}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{userPrincipalName}}) — {{#if accountEnabled}}Active{{else}}Disabled{{/if}} — Last sign-in: {{lastSignIn}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

**Identifier Lifecycle Management:**
- **Assignment:** Unique UPNs assigned upon account creation following naming convention [first.last]@{{primaryDomain}}. No identifier reuse for minimum 2 years after account deletion.
- **Selection:** Identifiers follow organizational naming standards ensuring uniqueness and traceability to individual personnel.
- **Disabling:** Accounts disabled within 24 hours of personnel termination per HR notification procedures. Disabled accounts retained for 90 days for audit purposes before deletion.
- **Reuse Prevention:** Deleted UPNs are blocked from reassignment for a minimum retention period.

{{#if cuiGroupExists}}
**CUI Access Identifiers:**
The "{{groupDisplayName}}" security group ({{memberCount}} members) tracks identifiers authorized for CUI access. Membership changes require approval from {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine user directory, account provisioning procedures, disabled account reports, identifier reuse policy documentation, and CUI group membership logs.

